  "description": "The FIFTH arm of the ten-way selection EVALUATE TRUE at :148-182, and the only case in this folder that types a LOWER-CASE selector. SEL0001I through SEL0004I all arrive as spaces, so :149, :152, :155 and :158 are each evaluated and each false, and only then does :161 match - an EVALUATE TRUE stops at its first true WHEN, so the four failures ahead of the match are part of the behaviour being pinned and arms six to ten at :164-178 and WHEN OTHER at :179 are never evaluated at all (gate G30). The arm tests 'NOT = SPACES AND LOW-VALUES', which a lower-case 's' satisfies exactly as an upper-case 'S' would. :162 then moves the cell into CDEMO-CT00-TRN-SEL-FLG and :163 moves TRNID05I - not TRNID04I and not TRNID06I - into CDEMO-CT00-TRN-SELECTED. That is the MIDDLE of the ten-row table, which case18 brackets at the first element and case14 at the last: an off-by-one in either direction lands on a neighbour here rather than falling off the end, so the middle row is where a 1-based-to-0-based slip hides instead of failing loudly. THE FLAG IS NOT CASE-NORMALISED. :162 copies the received byte verbatim and COTRN00C contains no FUNCTION UPPER-CASE anywhere - its only intrinsic is FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE at :569 - so CDEMO-CT00-TRN-SEL-FLG comes back as the lower-case 's' that was typed. Some sibling programs do fold case; this one does not, and that asymmetry is an inherited characteristic preserved rather than tidied (practice B5). Both cursor fields being present, :183-184 is true and the inner EVALUATE at :185 reaches WHEN 's' at :187 - the LOWER half of a two-clause fall-through pair whose upper half is WHEN 'S' at :186. The two clauses share ONE body, so the downstream effect is byte-identical to the upper-case path, and WHEN OTHER at :196 is a third and distinct arm that this case does not reach (case17 drives it with a selector that is neither letter). The shared body runs in source order: :188 hard-codes COTRN01C into CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM, :189 stamps WS-TRANID from :37, :190 stamps WS-PGMNAME from :36, :191 MOVEs 0 to CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT and :192-195 XCTLs. In a stateless translation that transfer is a response field naming the next program and nothing more - no server-side forward, no redirect and no session - with the 160-byte communication area and the 58-byte CDEMO-CT00-INFO extension of :62-70 both travelling in the payload as separate members, never folded together (gates G37 and G40, rule R6). The inbound values are chosen so that every one of the four overwrites is observable rather than merely asserted: CM00 becomes CT00, COMEN01C becomes COTRN00C, COTRN00C becomes COTRN01C and the context 1 becomes 0, while the customer, account and card identifiers pass through untouched because COTRN00C writes none of them. CONTROL LEAVES AT :193, so everything after it is unreached: the TRNIDINI edit at :206-219, the MOVE -1 at :221, the page reset at :224 and PROCESS-PAGE-FORWARD at :225. The page number therefore comes back as the 1 it arrived as rather than the 0 that :224 would have moved, the next-page flag as the Y it arrived as, no STARTBR, READNEXT, READPREV or ENDBR is issued against TRANSACT even though twenty-four records are seeded, no map is sent so POPULATE-HEADER-INFO at :571-586 never runs and the header is not refreshed, and both message channels hold the spaces :102-103 left. The cursor is still TRNIDINL because :105 sets it in MAIN-PARA before any branch is taken, not because :221 ran. Two mandated class names diverge from their sources and both are honoured verbatim under rule R1: COTRN00C LISTS transactions although the migrated class is TransactionMenuController, and COTRN01C VIEWS the selected transaction although its class is TransactionAddController - the COTRN01C source header and README.md both document CT01 as Transaction View (risk R-B). This case asserts the HANDOFF only and assumes nothing about an insert at the target. No user-specified rules govern this fixture - review_rules reports none - so enterprise practice binds instead. Statically derived by reading app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl paragraph by paragraph and cross-checking app/cpy/CVTRA05Y.cpy for the 350-byte record and its FILLER, app/cpy-bms/COTRN00.CPY for the xxxI widths, app/bms/COTRN00.bms for the DFHMDF lengths and app/cpy/COCOM01Y.cpy for the 160-byte communication area - never captured from a running COBOL program, because executing the legacy code is impossible in this environment (practice B12, risk R-A).",
